From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FirebirdTA01 <FirebirdTA01@aol.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 09:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] spu: every address is mode dependent

lq and stq ignore the low four address bits and move a whole quadword,
and a value narrower than 16 bytes lives in the preferred slot of its
register, so the bytes an address names depend on the mode of the
access.  SPU did not define TARGET_MODE_DEPENDENT_ADDRESS_P, so generic
code treated (mem:SI A+4) as the low part of (mem:DI A).  Before reload
spu_split_load turns such a narrowed load into a quadword load and a
rotate, but late-combine (GCC 15) also runs after reload: it folded a
DImode stack reload into the SImode truncation that used it, through
simplify_truncation's truncate-of-MEM rule, and "return (int) u64;"
returned the high word (libsheap cellSheapQueryFree).  With the hook
returning true, late-combine runs at its GCC 16 default on SPU again.
---
diff --git a/gcc/config/spu/spu.cc b/gcc/config/spu/spu.cc
index 693524a..285d782 100644
--- a/gcc/config/spu/spu.cc
+++ b/gcc/config/spu/spu.cc
@@ -3601,6 +3601,27 @@ spu_addr_space_legitimate_address_p (machine_mode mode, rtx x,
   return spu_legitimate_address_p (mode, x, reg_ok_strict);
 }
 
+/* Implement TARGET_MODE_DEPENDENT_ADDRESS_P.  Every SPU address is mode
+   dependent: lq and stq ignore the low four address bits and move the
+   whole quadword, and a value narrower than 16 bytes lives in the preferred
+   slot of the register (bytes 0-3, or the low bytes of word 0 for QImode
+   and HImode).  So the bytes an address names depend on the mode of the
+   access: the big-endian lowpart (mem:SI A+4) of (mem:DI A) loads the high
+   word of the DImode value, not its low word.  Returning true stops generic
+   code from narrowing or widening a MEM in place (simplify_truncation of a
+   MEM, simplify_subreg of a MEM, combine's extraction narrowing, convert_move,
+   reload of a SUBREG of a pseudo with a memory equivalent); it keeps the
+   access in its own mode and narrows the value in registers instead.  Before
+   reload spu_split_load rewrites such a narrowed MEM as a quadword load and a
+   rotate, but late-combine (GCC 15) also runs after reload, where it does
+   not, and "return (int) u64;" returned the high word.  */
+static bool
+spu_mode_dependent_address_p (const_rtx addr ATTRIBUTE_UNUSED,
+			      addr_space_t as ATTRIBUTE_UNUSED)
+{
+  return true;
+}
+
 /* When the address is reg + const_int, force the const_int into a
    register.  */
 static rtx
@@ -7395,6 +7416,9 @@ TARGET_GNU_ATTRIBUTES (spu_attribute_table,
 #undef TARGET_LEGITIMATE_ADDRESS_P
 #define TARGET_LEGITIMATE_ADDRESS_P spu_legitimate_address_p
 
+#undef TARGET_MODE_DEPENDENT_ADDRESS_P
+#define TARGET_MODE_DEPENDENT_ADDRESS_P spu_mode_dependent_address_p
+
 #undef TARGET_LEGITIMATE_CONSTANT_P
 #define TARGET_LEGITIMATE_CONSTANT_P spu_legitimate_constant_p
 
